Q: Simple group by query by using MongoDB Compass A: <p>you can use <a href="https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/reference/method/db.collection.aggregate/" rel="noreferrer">Mongodb Aggregation pipeline</a> with <a href="https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/group" rel="noreferrer">$group</a> with <a href="https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/sum/" rel="noreferrer">$sum</a> to achieve this.</p>

<p><strong>Try :</strong> </p>

<pre><code>db.collection_name.aggregate([{
    $group : {
        _id : "$subject",
        subject : {$first : "$subject"},
        count : {$sum : 1}
    }
}])
</code></pre>

Q: CKEditor in my React Project -&gt; Drop down view doesn&#39;t appear correctly A: <p>apply that to your global CSS</p>
<pre><code>
.ck-body-wrapper {
    z-index: 9999 !important;
}
.ck.ck-dropdown__panel {
    z-index: 10000 !important;
}
</code></pre>
<p>the issue might be in your Zindex so give that a higher value</p>
